Ticket **#4471** took in **412** unique date reports and treated them as one known parser bug.
The cause table disagrees: the same queue holds **two** problems. Intake tags and subject-line
dedupe hid the split.

<Callout kind="warn">
Merged as one. Filed again as two — one GitHub ticket per cause, with its report count.
</Callout>

## What #4471 actually holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Tickets filed (this repo)

| cause | reports | GitHub issue | desk outcome (05 Oct) |
| --- | ---: | --- | --- |
| `parser` | 379 | [#1](https://github.com/vertexbz/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1) | fixed — `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales` |
| `hint` | 33 | [#2](https://github.com/vertexbz/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2) | won't fix — booking-v3 form retired |

`parser` is every day-first tenant where the shared parser still reads month first (app, email,
and booking-v2 form traffic). `hint` is only booking-v3 form traffic: the field prints
`MM/DD/YYYY` while the tenant still reads day first, so people type month-first and the form
flips it.

Five reports under `parser` were read on the desk as a one-day move; they stay with that cause
by tenant.

## Why the old page was wrong

The incident page for #4471 called this known and one fix. Subject-line merge made that look
true. The components in this kb already know better — they group by tenant locale and form,
not by intake tag.

